Manage the reusable cache policies

Usage:
  nexoctl cache policy [flags]
  nexoctl cache policy [command]

Available Commands:
  create      Define a cache policy
  edit        Change a defined cache policy
  export      Export the defined cache policies as YAML
  import      Create or replace the cache policies of a YAML file
  info        Show a cache policy and the Cache-Control it sends
  list        List the cache policies, built-in and defined
  remove      Remove a defined cache policy no setting names

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for policy

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl cache policy [command] --help" for more information about a command.
